course: dictionary
lesson: 3649
title: Breaking words apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compound word is two smaller words joined together, and the parts often show the meaning. Fire plus place makes fireplace: a place for a fire. Check your idea by putting it into the sentence.
explain: «Christmas decorations are kept away from fireplaces and candles because they catch fire.» The clue is catch fire. A fireplace is where the fire is, so decorations must be kept away from it. Swap in your meaning: "kept away from a place for a fire" still makes sense.
explain: «Weasels dive under the tables and leap for the windows; ferrets rush for the fireplace and get stuck in the chimney.» The chimney is the clue. A fireplace sits at the bottom of a chimney, so the ferrets have run into the opening where the fire would be.
fact: A fireplace is an open space at the bottom of a chimney, inside a room.
fact: A fire is lit in the fireplace to heat the room.
fact: In the past, fireplaces were the main place for heating and cooking.
fact: Keep children back from the fireplace, and use a fireguard around the fire.
fact: «By the fireplace» tells you where something is, and «a stone fireplace» tells you what it is made of.
exercise: What is a fireplace? | A tall tree in the garden | *An open space at the bottom of a chimney, where a fire is lit to heat a room | A kind of chimney sweep | A bed for a cat
exercise: Why must children be kept back from the fireplace? | To make them sleepy | *To keep them safe from the fire | So they can cook their tea | Because it is too cold to go near it
exercise: Find and copy one word from «a stone fireplace» that tells you what it is made of. | fireplace | *stone | the | a
test: Which two smaller words make up fireplace? | fire and face | *fire and place | fir and replace | fireman and lace
test: What does a fireplace do for a room? | Lets the sun in | *Heats the room | Makes the room wet | Keeps the room dark
exam: Why is a fireguard put around a fireplace? | *To keep people back from the fire | To stop the room getting light | To keep the cat warm and dry | To hold up the chimney
